  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Statement pages p1-p4; the governmental funds statements (p3-p4) in the trim show only the Total, General, Road-Bridge and Special Road columns (the Inheritance Tax and Nonmajor columns are not in the trim); totals tie. Beginning balances are printed as cash basis fund balance (beginning_cash left null); ending cash from the p3 Cash and Cash Equivalents line. Statement 'Taxes' 2,630,317 split: Inheritance Tax Fund 355,399 (p7) and Visitor Promotion/Improvement 2,896 each (p8) by fund name; General Fund 2,260,054 + 911 Fund 9,072 stay unlabeled (no printed tax-type breakdown). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p5), major fund budget schedules (p6-7) and nonmajor fund budget schedules (p10-13); the nonmajor combining statement (p8-9) is not recorded separately to avoid double counting, but its function rows were used to categorize each fund's single Disbursements line. Expenditure detail lines print no actual-column totals separately from the single line, so expenditure detail_totals are only given for the General Fund. Zero-actual lines are kept only where a budget is printed. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
